<title>LEBANON: Most Lebanese t-bill yields fall.</title>
<headline>Most Lebanese t-bill yields fall.</headline>
<dateline>BEIRUT 1997-02-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Most yields fell on Lebanese treasury bills, according to weekly rates issued by the Bank of Lebanon on Monday.</p>
<p>It announced the following interest rates for its February 20 issues (previous week in brackets):</p>
<p>    Term		     Discount		     Yield</p>
<p>				(percent)		   (percent)</p>
<p>    Three months	  13.41 (13.45)	     13.87 (13.92)</p>
<p>    Six months	    13.64 (13.73)	     14.64 (14.74)</p>
<p>    12 months	     13.30 (13.30)	     15.33 (15.33)</p>
<p>    24 months   (Interest payable twice yearly) 16.18 (16.30)</p>
<p>-Beirut editorial (961 1) 602057 745307 745308</p>
</text>
